commits.message:
deploy: name rel/parts in worktree walk for readability

Use named rel/parts instead of reconstructing the path via Path(*p);
split the two skip sets onto their own lines. No behavior change.

what a run of every co wiki command on a real notebook found (#1670)

Every command was run against a copy of a real 90-day notebook. Fixed here:
- investigations were missing from `co wiki logs` and `logs --usage`; each is
  now a run record with its cost (not charged to the background daily cap);
- an error that names a command now makes it the Next line (`sync` before
  `start` said "run co wiki start" and printed Next: co wiki logs);
- `start` exits 1 when its first update fails, instead of 0 with the failure
  nested in the output;
- maintenance may cite the page that existed before it, as investigation may;
  a real pass was refused for citing the map's own email line;
- the daily round tries the next page when the busiest one needs more calls
  than the day has left, instead of failing every day and reaching no one;
- `investigate --list` without a category is refused, as its page says;
- errors for an unknown source or setting list the valid names;
- titles name the whole command ("Wiki sources add"), an empty usage report
  says so, skills --list drops a meaningless count, and init no longer points
  at `unfinished`.

